# Pocket Agent Extension Overview

This repository contains the VS Code extension component of the Pocket Agent system for remotely controlling Cursor's AI chat sessions.

## Extension Architecture

The VS Code extension captures chat data from Cursor and communicates with a separate web frontend for remote monitoring and control.

### Key Files

- [src/cursor-plugin.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/cursor-plugin.js) - Main extension entry point and CDP integration
- [src/config.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/config.js) - Configuration management with VS Code settings
- [src/constants.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/constants.js) - Constants including server URLs and OAuth scopes
- [src/cdpHelper.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/cdpHelper.js) - Chrome DevTools Protocol helpers
- [src/logger.js](mdc:pocket-agent/src/logger.js) - Logging utilities
- [package.json](mdc:pocket-agent/package.json) - Extension manifest and dependencies

## Core Functionality

### Chrome DevTools Protocol Integration
- Connects to Cursor's debug port (default: 9223)
- Extracts chat HTML content from active windows
- Injects messages back into Cursor chat interface

### Authentication
- GitHub OAuth integration via VS Code API
- Service token exchange with frontend
- JWT-based API authentication

### Configuration
- VS Code settings integration
- Environment variable support
- Configurable server URL and debug port

## API Communication

The extension communicates with the frontend via HTTP endpoints:

- `POST /api/auth/vscode/github-exchange` - Token exchange
- `POST /api/chat/update` - Send chat data
- `GET /api/commands/poll-outgoing/[windowId]` - Poll for commands

